   4.002077317154505*^9},ExpressionUUID->"b29eda7f-af1d-421c-854d-\
7ce27c5e97ca"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The elliptic curve E de\[FiLigature]ned by the normal cubic equation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["y", "2"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e15f19c-5bd7-4bb7-af71-fcc9c511e30e"],
 " + y = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", "3"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "984fba13-3f03-4835-b9c9-8afaebcc7fbc"],
 " \[Minus] x has six obvious points on it (0, 0), (1, 0), (\[Minus]1, 0), \
(0, \[Minus]1), (1, \[Minus]1), and (\[Minus]1, \[Minus]1). If P = (0, 0), \
then these points are all in the subgroup generated by P as with P = (1, 1)."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.999734816084281*^9, 
  3.9997348527731113`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"de5dbd75-612a-4d50-b3dc-\
3fa923800c31"],

