Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Exercise 6", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.999735418324628*^9},ExpressionUUID->"22a018a2-5905-42a3-acac-\
50e380869f68"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let E denote the elliptic curve de\[FiLigature]ned by the cubic equation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["y", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c3363be9-b889-4d50-8511-a2b96f33d744"],
 " = x(x \[Minus] 1)(x + 9).\nFind a subgroup of order four in E(Q), show \
that (\[Minus]1, 4) = P is on E(Q) and not in this\nsubgroup, and calculate n \
P for n between \[Minus]7 and +7. Using Mazur\[CloseCurlyQuote]s theorem."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.999735444249838*^9, 3.99973545282611*^9}, 
   3.99973580305905*^9},ExpressionUUID->"1477f5e0-f01b-4ceb-9b18-\
e0cc528adbec"],

